  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High-value products derived from black soldier fly larvae raised on human waste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this project, Sanergy will use Aqua for All&#x2019;s funding to research and demonstrate the technical and business viability of high-value products, such as oil and protein meal, produced from black soldier fly larvae (BSFL) that are reared on faecal sludge. The circular economy for faecal sludge has remained constrained to low-value products, making it difficult to attract the private sector and commercial capital. Sanergy will research and test innovative waste processing methods and product lines derived from BSFL. This will provide sustainable and scalable solutions for developing countries across Africa and Asia where the implementation of sewage systems is unfeasible.Sanergy is in constant search to get its sanitation concept financially feasible. Income comes partly from the user fees and sale of end products, which is reducing the need for donations and government contributions. Increase of sales price for end products will make the concept more sustainable. Ring fencing the production lines will even make them bankable.In Kenya, Sanergy has developed an on-site shared sanitation concept for Low Income Areas, covering the entire chain from toiltet to end products derived from the fecal sludge. Revenues from the latter are essential to improve the business case of the concept. At present these products are compost (Evergrow), energy and chicken feed (KuZaPro). The latter is based on the larve of Blak Soldier Fly, raised in boxes with a mixture of fecal sludge and other organic waste. The sales price of this chicken feed is rather low. It is assumed that the revenues can increase if protein and fats are separately extracted from the larvae.At the start of the pilot, the daily production of Chicken meal was 10.25 tonnes against a sales price of &#x20ac; 1,10 per kg.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovate - Sanitation</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The focus of the Sanergy sanitation concept is on Low Income Areas with people that lack access to sanitation at household level. At the start of the project, Sanergy provided these sanitation services to over 100,000 people and is ready to scale. Hundreds of people get employment through this business. The client group for the end products range from chicken farmers (protein) and transport sector (oils) to high end consumers of cosmetics.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goals of this project are:1. to select the products that can be &apos;easily&apos; extracted from the larvae and have the best market prospects2. the select and pilot the best extraction methods and required equipment3. to prepare a marketing plan and business line for massive products&#x200b;The project covers 3 stages and a marketing survey. The 3 stages are:1 Literature research for product and production line selection1. Bench scale testing2. Production at pilot scaleBefore the 3rd phase, an external review is done to assure that the most appropriate products and equipment are selected.</narrative>
  </description>
